The first two lemmas below are templates for generated assertions: instantiate `lemma_1` for every generate index `i` with `0 <= i < NUM_REQ`, and `lemma_2` for every pair of generate indices satisfying `0 <= i < j < NUM_REQ`. Declare `lemma_3` at module scope.

After reset initialization, their conjunction with `prop` is 1-inductive. When requester `a` is granted, `ranks[a] == chosen_priority`. If requester `b` is requesting, the minimum-selection logic guarantees `chosen_priority <= ranks[b]`. Valid, distinct requester indices and pairwise distinct ranks strengthen this comparison to `ranks[a] < ranks[b]`.

These lemmas require `NUM_REQ >= 2`: for `NUM_REQ = 1`, the fallback assigns `another_arbitrary_requester = 1`, which is outside the array bounds.

